# The public GitHub mirrors, not ssh://git@git.graphdefined.com:5001/. Both
# carry the same commits, but only one of them can be reached without a
# credential: the internal host is not routable from GitHub Actions, and an SSH
# URL would need a deploy key for three repositories before the first clone
# succeeded. The conformance suites name the same URLs for the same reason.
#
# Whoever prefers to push through the internal host sets that per clone rather
# than here:
#
#     git config submodule.libs/Hermod.url ssh://git@git.graphdefined.com:5001/Vanaheimr/Hermod.git
#     git submodule sync libs/Hermod
#
# An existing checkout is not affected by this file at all - .git/config keeps
# the URL it was cloned with until `git submodule sync` is run.
#
# Why they are back: an application repository that cannot be cloned and built
# is an application repository that does not work. Reaching sideways for
# ..\..\Ratatoskr asked whoever cloned this to know, from a restore error
# naming three paths outside the tree, that four repositories go beside each
# other. One checkout is the whole build again, and the revisions are pinned,
# so a breaking change upstream no longer turns this red on its own.
#
# The layout under libs/ is the same side-by-side one, which is what lets the
# libraries keep reaching for each other unchanged: Ratatoskr finds Hermod at
# ..\..\Hermod, Hermod finds Styx at ..\..\Styx.
[submodule "libs/Styx"]
	path = libs/Styx
	url = https://github.com/Vanaheimr/Styx.git
[submodule "libs/Hermod"]
	path = libs/Hermod
	url = https://github.com/Vanaheimr/Hermod.git
[submodule "libs/Ratatoskr"]
	path = libs/Ratatoskr
	url = https://github.com/Vanaheimr/Ratatoskr.git
